+Material Smoothness Loss is a regularization term applied to material fields to enforce spatial smoothness by penalizing differences in material parameters between neighboring surface points [7299-material-smoothness-loss.md]. A specific variant, the BRDF Smoothness Loss, enforces smoothness of BRDF parameters using a normalized difference weighted by pseudo-albedo gradients [7299-material-smoothness-loss.md]. It differs from standard smoothness losses by incorporating a bilateral weight derived from rendered color and irradiance to modulate the penalty, ensuring smoothness is preserved across material boundaries [7299-material-smoothness-loss.md].
 
